#AUTO 94
#NEEDED 1
# eMMC wear / lifetime (issue 110n).
#
# The soldered-in eMMC reports how much of its rated write life it has used,
# in its EXT_CSD: a coarse health flag (PRE_EOL_INFO) and two 10%-step
# lifetime estimates (DEVICE_LIFE_TIME_EST_TYP_A/B). This probe reads and
# decodes them so we know how much life the internal flash has left — useful
# on a used device and before we start writing images back to it.
#
# Read-only; reuses the EXT_CSD read the fast-storage path already uses.
# Priority 94 sits right beside the other EXT_CSD probe (emmc-extcsd @ 95).

CALL emmc_init
CALL emmc_wear
